This was the concave/convex discussion. We came to the conclusion that the 
current way of drawing both wings is not wrong (perspective wise) and the 
artists likes the convex+concave wings more.

Just to explain the perspective: Get some tube and cut it to get something 
which looks like a halfpipe. Now take it and try get the same perspective used 
in the logo (put the "tube" horizontally in front of you, the open part of the 
"halfpipe" directly facing you and move your head slightly to the right). You 
will see that one end looks like a convex curve and the other one like a 
concave one.

